From bff63672bbe52a63c547177fa8cc890ff353c38e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the ZapProperty portal API: one platform key, every
 published listing

Company zt_live_ keys only ever see their own company's sites, so ZapProperty
(a cross-agency portal) could not show a listing published by a second
company. Add a platform-level key and a small read API for it.

- ZAPPROPERTY_API_KEY (config services.zapproperty.api_key); generate with
  `php artisan zapproperty:key` (prefix zp_live_). Unset = portal disabled (503).
- zapproperty.auth middleware: constant-time compare; company keys are
  rejected here and the portal key is rejected on company endpoints.
- GET  /api/v1/zapproperty/listings            active + show_on_zapproperty,
                                               all companies, + agent,
                                               meta.unpublished_total
- GET  /api/v1/zapproperty/listings/{id}       404 unless published
- GET  /api/v1/zapproperty/listings/{id}/photos/{photoId}
- GET/POST /api/v1/zapproperty/listings/{id}/tasks   re-enters the listing's
  company scope (acting as the site's creator) and delegates to TaskController
- Extract the asset payload into App\Support\AssetPayload so /assets and the
  portal return the same shape (photo URLs differ per route).
- Feature tests on Postgres; BUILDERS.md / PLATFORM_V2.md / .env.example.
